SUMMARY:Raatri- The Whispers of Night
DESCRIPTION:A Bharatnatyam performance celebrating night\, which is both sensual and formidable. As dusk gathers\, Radha\, adorned with stars\, goes to meet her beloved. She becomes night itself: seductress\, confidante\, and witness. \nThe piece opens in starlight and fragrance\, with the senses awakened and the god of love invited. In the embrace\, Radha’s adornments dissolve\, and she asks Krishna to dress her once more. When sleep brings dreams of war and death\, and the stillness of the night is broken by the approach of change. A keeper of secrets and a harbinger of loss\, the night is both lover and landscape in this performance. \nCredits:\nMusic Composition: Sameer Rao & Srividya Ramnath\nVocals: Srividya Ramnath\nRhythm Composition\, Mridangam & Khanjeera: R. Sriganesh\nFlute: Sameer Rao\nViolin: Mattur Srinidhi\nVeena: Shubha Santhosh\nParai\, Urumi & Other percussions: Vishwa Bharath\nRecording Studio: Music Cloud \nSupported by: \n \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nA Bharatanatyam Solo\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdEmW1jmUnNAQep4UYeAh4arZsGIZhy1kw4GzzqgX7G9OhflA/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performer*: Anuradha Venkataraman\n*Event Categories*: Dance\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/raatri-the-whispers-of-night/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail-24.jpg
