SUMMARY:What's All the Song-and-Dance About?
DESCRIPTION:This event explores the emergence of Bharatanatyam in the early twentieth century\, told on stage through conversation\, music\, and dance. Who brought this art into modernity\, gesture by gesture? \nGenerations of women from professional dance communities sustained the practice\, but are rarely remembered today. Based on the book From the Corner of Her Eye: The Many Histories of Bharatanatyam\, the conversation shows Bharatanatyam to be a modern form that is also a refashioning of the dance that directly preceded it. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nHow Bharatanatyam Emerged\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSfQghY1HTfDeKQ_cFMop0eoaaAdbPcpdAcZUn0X9zTk6-Labg/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers & Performer*: Justin McCarthy\, Balakrishnan Raghavan\, Annapurna Garimella\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Dance\, History
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/whats-all-the-song-and-dance-about/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Dance,History
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ThumbnailWATSADA.jpg
END:VEVENT
