UID:98161-1796580000-1796585400@bangaloreinternationalcentre.org
SUMMARY:Cultivating Organisational Longevity
DESCRIPTION:This panel discussion looks at what keeps an organisation\, and the people within it\, healthy\, relevant\, and effective over time. Modern workplaces pursue growth\, agility\, and performance\, yet burnout\, toxic cultures\, and unsustainable ways of working can quietly shorten an organisation’s life. Can ambition coexist with care? \nThe event begins with an overview of current research on burnout\, workplace culture\, and sustainable performance\, followed by an introduction to the book Heal the Workplace and its RENEW framework for building healthier organisations. The panel consists of practitioners from organisational development\, psychotherapy\, social entrepreneurship\, healthcare innovation\, and business-building. They will consider how leaders can support recovery and honest conversation\, and how organisations can grow while caring for their people. \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nBuilding Workplaces That Thrive and Endure\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdQlGKzDPAVkGg2EeltMOh-AmT31WRU1lmXD9q7eNaaZuvzjA/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Subramanian Kalpathi\, Pranay Jivrajka\, Vishal Talreja\, Aruna Gopakumar\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Business\, Management
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/cultivating-organisational-longevity/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Business,Management
